 "notes": "All 28 seats have a winner; none uncalled. Virginia used its existing district lines (every incumbent ran in their old district number). Results are unofficial until certification; Virginia's elections commissioner noted the state itself does not declare winners. VA-01: Taylor 51.0%-48.7%; NBC projected, Axios reports AP call 5 Nov, Wittman conceded (Axios page itself returned 403 to me). VA-05: closest race, McGuire about 50.3%-48.0% (about 7,700 votes); AP called 5 Nov and Perriello conceded. VA-03, 08, 10, 11: winners rest on very large unofficial margins in Cardinal News' table (which itself makes no calls) plus FOX 5 DC / Virginia Business roundups naming them reelected; VA-03 source is the Cardinal News table only (Virginia Business snippet also says Scott won). MD-01: Harris 52.1%-47.7% in the state's unofficial count, reported as reelected by FOX 5 DC. MD rows other than Harris rest on the state's unofficial count (large margins); FOX 5 DC says Democrats won the other seven seats. WV: Telemundo page shows 99% counted but no explicit call; 270toWin says Decision Desk HQ called both WV seats for Republicans. KY-01/02/03/05: the Kentucky Lantern pages returned 403 when opened; the winners are taken from search-result text of those articles (and KY Secretary of State totals quoted in search results: Comer 154,910-74,260; Guthrie 145,139-81,112; Rogers 139,808-49,805). DE: AP call reported by FOX 29 live page; no vote totals seen. Backgrounds for new winners come from search-result text (Taylor: Henrico commonwealth's attorney; Gallrein: retired Navy SEAL/farmer per AP; Dembo: Lex18/Spectrum; Boafo: state delegate per primary coverage)."
